-- title:
--   Row-9 inverse-derivative residual coefficients
-- statement:
--   These are explicit finite coefficient data for the degree-9 inverse cubic of a fifth power of $z^3-z-\beta$. The algebraic parameter used in the later proofs satisfies $\alpha^3=1001/2-462\alpha+84\alpha^2$. The bundle defines the explicit degree-at-most-61 polynomial
--   $$J_\alpha(t)=\sum_{j=0}^{61}j_j(\alpha)t^j.$$
--   Each coefficient is a rational quadratic expression in $\alpha$. It is used in the separately proved identity $1-Q_\alpha(t)\partial_vG(t,P_\alpha(t))=t^{32}J_\alpha(t)$, which controls the Newton contraction.
-- source:
--   https://gist.github.com/Amal-David/adce933460b7501cb123f483f62775eb/f5a76eda649f3e995a8ec6b98387b23b64c6debb#file-fifth-md; H5_COMPLETE_CHAIN.md, Sections 1–4; lower/H5_LOWER_MIDDLE_COMPLETION.md and upper/H5_UPPER_BRIDGE.md in the archived research checkpoint. The finite Newton coefficient arrays are auxiliary exact certificates constructed for the accompanying Lean formalization, and are specified in full by this definition submission.

